	(text "Latching Flip Flop\nAn error is latched on the board, \nthe latch can be reset by toggling \nthe LVS. The UPS sends a pulse whenever \nLVS is toggled. Alternativly killing \nall power will reset too."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 95.25 170.434 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0332e409-8649-479d-838d-b23ea83758c3")
	)
	(text "0.5A Hold"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 424.18 346.456 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "05000e42-63ab-440a-8bcb-d20667826444")
	)
	(text "GREEN LIGHT LOGIC  (FS 2027 EV 4.10.3, 4.10.13-15)\n\nGREEN_ON = BELOW_HV_LIMIT AND all relays open (AIR+, AIR-, PRE ACT = HIGH)\n           AND NO_FAULT\n\nFault checks (any one -> PLAUSIBILITY_ERROR):\n 1-3. Relay check, per relay: INTENDED XOR ACTUAL\n      (stuck/welded relay, broken ACT wire once commanded closed)\n 4.   HV sense check: AIR+ AND AIR- commanded closed AND BELOW_HV_LIMIT\n      (HV expected but detector sees none -> TSAC sense wire open)\n\nPLAUSIBILITY_ERROR -> LTC6994 500 ms delay -> 74LVC1G74 latch\n - Error must last >500 ms (no trips from normal relay switching)\n - Latched fault: NO_FAULT LOW -> green off, FAULT LED on\n - Reset ONLY by LATCH_RST rising edge (UPS, LVS switched on)\n   and only if no error present. Open/stuck reset wire cannot clear it.\n - Power-on RC clears latch after full TSAL power-up\n\nSignal levels: ACT/INT HIGH = open (pull-ups); 12 V inputs pulled\ndown, so open wire / short to GND = LOW = light off"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 242.57 143.256 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0bc9f0f1-a377-4d97-8fe3-fcd085ebf950")
	)
	(text "200mA Hold"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 391.414 163.576 0)
		(effects
