	(text "The TSAL itself must have a red light, flashing continuously with a frequency between\n2 Hz and 5 Hz and a duty cycle of 50%, active when the LVS is active and for at least 15\nminutes after the LVS is switched off (see EV4.10.16), and the voltage across any DC-link capacitor exceeds\n\n 60VDC or 25VACRMS\n Half the nominal TS voltage\nwhichever is lower.\""
